        "original_id": "b0ad68de-0be5-54be-8885-169f439a978d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Iva Pacetti, Arrigo Boito\n- Works: Mefistofele\n- Places: Loew's Lexington Theatre, New York City, La Scala, Milan\n- Topics: opera premieres, performances\n\nFacts:\n- Mefistofele is the only completed opera composed by the Italian composer-librettist Arrigo Boito.\n- Mefistofele consists of a prologue, four acts, and an epilogue.\n- Mefistofele premiered on 5 March 1868 at La Scala in Milan.\n- Arrigo Boito conducted the premiere of Mefistofele despite lacking experience and skill as a conductor.\n- Iva Pacetti reprised a role the year after an earlier performance at Loew's Lexington Theatre in New York City.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "341d4b41-56e9-567b-a4f7-eee6a819a8b4",
        "text": "Page: Iva Pacetti. Sentence: She reprised the role the following year at Loew's Lexington Theatre in New York City.\nPage: Mefistofele. Sentence: Mefistofele (] ) is an opera in a prologue, four acts and an epilogue, the only completed opera with music by the Italian composer-librettist Arrigo Boito (there are several completed operas for which he was librettist only).\nPage: Mefistofele. Sentence: The opera was given its premiere on 5 March 1868 at La Scala, Milan, under the baton of the composer, despite his lack of experience and skill as a conductor.",
